            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We coordinate corporate pickups throughout Bakersfield, Oildale, Rosedale, Shafter, Delano, and Tehachapi. Our logistics fleet supports commercial offices, packing houses, and industrial operations across the entire Southern San Joaquin Valley corridor."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup scheduling take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most corporate pickups are scheduled within 3 to 5 business days from initial manifest confirmation. For large data center decommissioning projects or agricultural packaging refreshes, our logistical coordinators establish dedicated operational windows to minimize facility disruption."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, clients receive an itemized Certificate of Destruction and inventory report detailing serial numbers, equipment categories, and sanitization methods. This documentation provides complete audit support for HIPAA, GLBA, and Sarbanes-Oxley corporate compliance reviews."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup service free for businesses?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide complimentary scheduled pickup for organizations meeting qualifying inventory volumes. Our team evaluates your equipment manifest to coordinate logistics and identify hardware eligible for value recovery through remarked asset channels."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to our equipment after collection?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Assets undergo strict inventory intake and data sanitization before material reclamation. Obsolete equipment is separated into base commodities including steel, aluminum, and circuit boards under a strict zero landfill environmental commitment."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle enterprise data center projects?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS manages full-scale data center decommissioning, including server rack removal, structured cable dismantling, and enterprise UPS battery extraction with complete chain of custody validation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is data destruction HIPAA compliant for Bakersfield healthcare providers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, STS provides HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312 compliant data destruction for Bakersfield healthcare facilities including Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield. We execute Business Associate Agreements and provide serialized certificates of destruction for OCR audit readiness."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do Bakersfield businesses recover value from retired IT equipment?",
